WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.448
Module three. How the admin approves a vendor's KYC.

2
00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:10.366
This module is for the Oribrix team members who approve vendors.

3
00:00:10.816 --> 00:00:13.483
We'll start with the KYC lifecycle page.

4
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:16.344
Then how to review each document properly.

5
00:00:16.794 --> 00:00:19.503
How to approve custom categories and warehouses.

6
00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:23.068
The final approval step, which people often forget.

7
00:00:23.518 --> 00:00:25.928
And what the vendor sees once they're approved.

8
00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:33.926
In the admin panel, open KYC Lifecycle. At the top you see the total applications,

9
00:00:33.926 --> 00:00:38.360
And these three numbers. The figures here are from the demo data.

10
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:42.991
Pending verification is your work queue. These vendors are waiting for you.

11
00:00:43.441 --> 00:00:45.041
Approved vendors are live.

12
00:00:45.491 --> 00:00:48.449
And suspended vendors have been blocked by an admin.

13
00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:51.806
We'll see where the suspend button is later in this module.

14
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.037
Approving a vendor always takes these five steps.

15
00:00:57.487 --> 00:01:00.325
Open the vendor from the pending verification list.

16
00:01:00.775 --> 00:01:02.993
Review each document, one by one.

17
00:01:03.443 --> 00:01:08.265
Approve or reject the custom categories, and approve the registration warehouse.

18
00:01:08.715 --> 00:01:10.635
Then do the final vendor approval.

19
00:01:11.085 --> 00:01:14.391
And the vendor automatically gets an email with their login.

20
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.720
Let's watch this in the live demo.

21
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:27.592
This is the KYC lifecycle page. The new vendor, oribrix, shows as pending

22
00:01:27.592 --> 00:01:31.845
Verification, with GSTIN and PAN visible in the list.

23
00:01:38.533 --> 00:01:42.586
The eye icon on the right opens the full KYC details.

24
00:01:54.533 --> 00:01:59.625
Each document has its own card. Click it to open the file in a separate window, so

25
00:01:59.625 --> 00:02:01.488
You can check it side by side.

26
00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:13.331
Choose the status from the dropdown, add a remark if needed, and click Update doc

27
00:02:13.331 --> 00:02:16.154
Status. A small message confirms the update.

28
00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:34.960
Opening a document isn't enough. Here's what to actually check.

29
00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:41.420
On the GST certificate, the business name and GSTIN must match what the vendor typed

30
00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.279
In the form.

31
00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:45.545
On the business PAN, the number and the name should match.

32
00:02:45.995 --> 00:02:50.538
On the cancelled cheque, the account number and IFSC must match the banking step.

33
00:02:50.538 --> 00:02:52.502
This protects the vendor's payouts.

34
00:02:52.952 --> 00:02:56.493
On the Aadhaar, the name should match the authorised signatory.

35
00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.866
For optional documents, check the validity dates.

36
00:03:00.316 --> 00:03:03.805
And every file must be clear, complete, and not expired.

37
00:03:03.805 --> 00:03:08.976
If anything is wrong, reject that document with a clear remark, so the vendor knows

38
00:03:08.976 --> 00:03:09.724
What to fix.

39
00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:15.098
Scroll down, and you reach categories and warehouses.

40
00:03:15.548 --> 00:03:19.026
The standard categories the vendor picked are shown for reference.

41
00:03:19.476 --> 00:03:24.084
Custom category requests need a decision. Approve or reject each one.

42
00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:27.350
The registration warehouse needs approval too.

43
00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:31.759
Before approving it, check that the map pin really matches the address.

44
00:03:31.759 --> 00:03:34.882
Customers near that pin will see this vendor's products.

45
00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:39.187
Let's watch this in the live demo.

46
00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.650
Here you see the owner details, bank details, and on the right, categories and

47
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:47.277
Warehouses.

48
00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:58.104
The custom category request has Approve and Reject buttons.

49
00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:03.331
In the demo the name showed as object object, a display bug the team is fixing.

50
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:16.854
The registration warehouse, Central City, is approved here, so its status changes

51
00:04:16.854 --> 00:04:18.413
From pending to approved.

52
00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:39.433
Now, the most important step in this module. Approving every document is not enough.

53
00:04:39.433 --> 00:04:44.354
The vendor is still pending. You must go to Vendor action, choose Approved, and

54
00:04:44.354 --> 00:04:49.525
Click Update status. Only then is the vendor's registration approved, and only then

55
00:04:49.525 --> 00:04:54.633
Do they get their login email. If a vendor says, I uploaded everything but I can't

56
00:04:54.633 --> 00:04:56.813
Log in, this is usually the reason.

57
00:05:45.533 --> 00:05:47.453
Let's watch this in the live demo.

58
00:05:50.467 --> 00:05:55.541
First, the vendor's screen. All five documents are in, progress shows one hundred

59
00:05:55.541 --> 00:05:58.360
Percent, but verification is still In review.

60
00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:12.496
Back in admin, a green note says all uploaded items are reviewed, and you can now

61
00:06:12.496 --> 00:06:14.755
Approve or reject the registration.

62
00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:25.589
Vendor action is set to Approved, and Update status is clicked.

63
00:06:25.589 --> 00:06:30.819
Notice the Suspend vendor button that appears. That's how a vendor is blocked later.

64
00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:43.534
On the vendor side: Your account is verified. The dashboard is unlocked.

65
00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:57.123
And here is the vendor dashboard, ready for them to add stock.

66
00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:06.584
So you have three tools. When do you use which?

67
00:07:07.034 --> 00:07:11.392
Reject a single document when the file is wrong, blurry or expired.

68
00:07:11.392 --> 00:07:15.034
Always add a clear remark, and the vendor can re-upload.

69
00:07:15.484 --> 00:07:20.431
Approve the vendor only when all mandatory documents are approved, the categories

70
00:07:20.431 --> 00:07:23.058
Are decided, and the warehouse is approved.

71
00:07:23.508 --> 00:07:27.866
Suspend is for later, if there's a serious problem with an approved vendor.

72
00:07:27.866 --> 00:07:31.294
It blocks them, so use it with care, and tell your manager.

73
00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:37.399
A rejection without a clear remark just creates a phone call.

74
00:07:37.399 --> 00:07:39.460
Here are examples of good remarks.

75
00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:45.149
For a GST certificate: the name on the certificate doesn't match the business name,

76
00:07:45.149 --> 00:07:47.547
Please upload the correct certificate.

77
00:07:47.997 --> 00:07:52.471
For a cancelled cheque: the account number doesn't match the bank details, please

78
00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:52.968
Re-check.

79
00:07:53.418 --> 00:07:58.313
For an Aadhaar: the image is blurry and the name isn't readable, please upload a

80
00:07:58.313 --> 00:07:58.986
Clear scan.

81
00:07:59.436 --> 00:08:04.256
And for a warehouse: the map pin is in a different city from the address, please

82
00:08:04.256 --> 00:08:07.329
Move the pin. Specific, polite, and easy to act on.

83
00:08:09.733 --> 00:08:13.552
Why be so careful? Because every approval has consequences later.

84
00:08:14.002 --> 00:08:17.308
Wrong bank details mean payouts go to the wrong account.

85
00:08:17.758 --> 00:08:21.918
A wrong GSTIN means invoices and tax filings go wrong.

86
00:08:22.368 --> 00:08:26.668
A wrong warehouse pin means customers in the wrong area see this vendor, and

87
00:08:26.668 --> 00:08:27.574
Deliveries fail.

88
00:08:28.024 --> 00:08:32.377
And approving a fake vendor means failed orders and unhappy customers.

89
00:08:32.377 --> 00:08:34.616
When in doubt, ask before approving.

90
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.261
Use this checklist every single time.

91
00:08:39.711 --> 00:08:44.021
GSTIN and business name match the GST certificate.

92
00:08:44.471 --> 00:08:46.476
The cheque matches the bank details.

93
00:08:46.926 --> 00:08:49.294
The Aadhaar name matches the signatory.

94
00:08:49.744 --> 00:08:52.880
Every custom category is approved or rejected.

95
00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.527
The warehouse pin is checked and approved.

96
00:08:55.977 --> 00:08:59.476
And finally, vendor action Approved, then Update status.

97
00:09:01.867 --> 00:09:06.089
Approval isn't the finish line. Here's what should happen on the vendor's first day,

98
00:09:06.089 --> 00:09:07.798
And you can guide them through it.

99
00:09:08.248 --> 00:09:11.896
The login email arrives at the signatory's email address.

100
00:09:12.346 --> 00:09:15.098
The vendor logs in, and changes their password.

101
00:09:15.548 --> 00:09:18.257
If needed, they add staff accounts for their team.

102
00:09:18.707 --> 00:09:22.063
The admin makes sure the warehouse is verified in Shiprocket.

103
00:09:22.063 --> 00:09:23.934
You'll learn this in module seven.

104
00:09:24.384 --> 00:09:28.202
And the vendor adds their first SKUs, which is module five.

105
00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:35.504
Quick check. All the documents show approved, but the vendor says they can't log in.

106
00:09:35.504 --> 00:09:37.256
What's the most likely reason?

107
00:09:41.206 --> 00:09:46.457
Right, the final vendor approval wasn't done. Open the vendor, set Vendor action to

108
00:09:46.457 --> 00:09:48.609
Approved, and click Update status.

109
00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:52.893
Let's sum up module three.

110
00:09:53.343 --> 00:09:57.269
Work from the pending verification list in KYC lifecycle.

111
00:09:57.719 --> 00:10:01.068
Open every document and match it to what the vendor typed.

112
00:10:01.518 --> 00:10:04.462
If you reject something, always add a clear remark.

113
00:10:04.912 --> 00:10:06.917
Approve the categories and the warehouse.

114
00:10:07.367 --> 00:10:11.350
And always finish with vendor action Approved, and Update status.

115
00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:14.535
In the next module, we'll build the product catalog.

116
00:10:16.933 --> 00:10:22.096
That's the end of module 3. Next up, module 4: Admin: product catalog.
